# The honest retry history (good/retry-recorded-honestly.hist) with the two
# attempts collapsed into ONE logical put — what a client library that hid
# its retries would report. A single put of A cannot be both before op 2 and
# after op 4. Without deduplication (Phase 13) a client must not present an
# unknown-then-retried write as one operation.
1 c1 put "k" 1 9 ok value="A"
2 c3 get "k" 2 3 ok output="A"
3 c2 put "k" 4 5 ok value="B"
4 c3 get "k" 6 7 ok output="B"
6 c3 get "k" 10 11 ok output="A"
